NET - network status
Usage: net [status|scan|up|down]

Reports the network peripheral CloverOS can see. On CC:Tweaked the network
is whichever peripheral is attached, so a computer with a modem shows
"modem" and one with a wifi card shows "wifi".

status   (default) show interface, status, signal strength and peripherals
scan     rescan the hardware and show what is attached
up       open the network peripheral
down     close the network peripheral

Examples:
  net
  net up
  net scan

Notes:
- A computer with no network peripheral reports "interface: none".
- "up"/"down" need a peripheral that supports opening; several CC:Tweaked
  builds always report online and refuse to be closed.
